# User Search and Role Filter

Goal
Add keyword search and role filtering to the user list. Search and filtering must work together with the pagination introduced in PR 1.

API
Endpoint: GET /api/users

Add these query parameters:

q — keyword used to search display name, username, or email.
role — filter users by role.
page — page number; default: 1.
limit — users per page; default: 10.
sort — sorting field; default: username.
order — asc or desc; default: asc.
Search and role filtering must be combinable. Pagination metadata must reflect the filtered/search results, not the total number of users.

Example:

GET /api/users?q=john&role=1&page=1&limit=10

Search Behavior
The q parameter should search across:

displayName
username
email
The search should be case-insensitive.

If no users match the search or filter, return 200 with an empty data array and appropriate pagination metadata.

Role Filter
The role parameter filters users by their role.

The filter should use the application's existing role values and should not expose or modify protected user information.

Response
The existing paginated response format from PR 1 remains unchanged:

{
"data": [],
"pagination": {
"page": 1,
"limit": 10,
"totalItems": 5,
"totalPages": 1,
"hasNextPage": false,
"hasPreviousPage": false
}
}

User Page
The /users page must provide:

A keyword search input.
A role filter.
Paginated results.
Previous and Next controls.
Results updated according to the selected search/filter criteria.
Search, role filtering, and pagination should work together without requiring separate pages.

Validation and Documentation
Validate and sanitize the search input.
Validate the role value.
Return 400 for invalid query parameters.
Return 200 with an empty result for valid searches with no matches.
Document all query parameters and their possible values in Swagger.
Preserve the existing authentication and authorization rules.
Out of Scope
This PR does not change:

User creation.
User editing or deletion.
Authentication.
User roles themselves.
The existing pagination response structure.
